WEBVTT

00:00.800 --> 00:02.739
Meet Thiri.

00:02.689 --> 00:06.412
She found the phone she had saved for months to buy.

00:06.412 --> 00:08.925
The seller looked real.

00:08.925 --> 00:11.560
The price felt possible.

00:11.560 --> 00:14.557
So they moved to private chat.

00:14.557 --> 00:16.869
She paid first.

00:16.869 --> 00:19.853
There was no protected payment.

00:19.853 --> 00:22.635
No verified identity.

00:22.635 --> 00:25.847
No record of the phone's condition.

00:25.847 --> 00:28.119
The package arrived.

00:28.119 --> 00:30.605
The phone did not work.

00:30.605 --> 00:33.710
Her messages went unanswered.

00:33.710 --> 00:36.022
The money was gone.

00:36.022 --> 00:42.191
And Thiri had no evidence, no support, and no safe way to fight back.

00:42.191 --> 00:47.138
In Myanmar, a good deal should not require blind trust.

00:47.138 --> 00:50.592
What if second-hand could feel first-choice?
